# Words CONFIG_CMDLINE must carry (check-kernel-config.sh). Linux 6.2
# removed the Kconfig options for these two; the parameters are all there is.

random.trust_cpu=off         a generator inside the CPU cannot be examined, so RDRAND is mixed in without being credited (docs/OWN-RANDOMNESS.md §3.3)
random.trust_bootloader=off  the firmware's seed was chosen by the firmware; mixed in, not credited

# Words CONFIG_CMDLINE must carry as well (check-kernel-config.sh).

efi=disable_early_pci_dma  no PCI device the firmware left running can write to memory before the kernel has set up the IOMMU (docs/IMAGES.md §1)

console=ttynull  the kernel's console is the null one: with no console= word it would take the 16550 serial port, and kernel lines, a panic's message included, would leave on COM1
